    {
      "content": {
        "note": {
          "text": "## Why line 11 samples\n\nWith $E_i \\sim \\mathrm{Exp}(1)$ drawn for every token $i$,\n\n$$\n\\Pr\\Big[\\arg\\max_i \\frac{p_i}{E_i} = k\\Big] = p_k\n$$\n\nso dividing by exponential noise and taking the largest is the same as drawing from $p$, without a cumulative sum.\n\n| temperature | what it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\to 0$ | always the likeliest token |\n| $1$ | the model's own distribution |\n| $> 1$ | flatter, more surprising |"
        }
      },
